.IX Title "SSL_ADD_CERT_COMPRESSION_ALG 3"
.TH SSL_ADD_CERT_COMPRESSION_ALG 3 "2024-08-31" "1.1.1h" "OpenSSL"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
SSL_cert_compress_cb_fn, SSL_cert_decompress_cb_fn, SSL_add_cert_compression_alg, SSL_CTX_add_cert_compression_alg, SSL_get_cert_compression_compress_id, SSL_get_cert_compression_decompress_id \&\- TLS certificate compression methods
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\& #include <openssl/ssl.h>
\&
\& typedef int (*SSL_cert_compress_cb_fn)(SSL *s,
\&                    const unsigned char *in, size_t inlen,
\&                    unsigned char *out, size_t *outlen);
\& typedef int (*SSL_cert_decompress_cb_fn)(SSL *s,
\&                    const unsigned char *in, size_t inlen,
\&                    unsigned char *out, size_t outlen);
\&
\& int SSL_add_cert_compression_alg(SSL *s, int alg_id,
\&                                 SSL_cert_compress_cb_fn compress,
\&                                 SSL_cert_decompress_cb_fn decompress);
\& int SSL_CTX_add_cert_compression_alg(SSL_CTX *ctx, int alg_id,
\&                                     SSL_cert_compress_cb_fn compress,
\&                                     SSL_cert_decompress_cb_fn decompress);
\&
\& int SSL_get_cert_compression_compress_id(SSL *s);
\& int SSL_get_cert_compression_decompress_id(SSL *s);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBSSL_cert_compress_cb_fn\fR is a pointer to a function that performs compression.
It must write the compressed representation of \fBin\fR to \fBout\fR. \fBinlen\fR is
the byte length of the buffer \fBin\fR. \fB*outlen\fR is the total size of the buffer
\&\fBout\fR. Upon exit, \fB*outlen\fR is the actual size of the compressed buffer
\&\fBout\fR. Note that if \fBout\fR is \s-1NULL,\s0 it only computes the length of the
compressed buffer \fBout\fR and write it to \fB*outlen\fR. It returns 1 on success
or 0 on error.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_cert_decompress_cb_fn\fR is a pointer to a function that performs
decompression. The compressed data is passed as \fBin\fR with length \fBinlen\fR
and the decompressed result must be exactly \fBoutlen\fR bytes long. It returns
1 on success, in which case \fB*out\fR must be set to the result of decompressing
\&\fBin\fR, or 0 on error.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_add_cert_compression_alg()\fR registers a certificate compression algorithm
on \fBs\fR with algorithm identifier \fBalg_id\fR. The compress callback \fBcompress\fR
is used to compress the Certificate message, and decompress callback
\&\fBdecompress\fR is used to decompress compressed Certificate message in
CompressedCertificate message. These callbacks can be \s-1NULL.\s0 Algorithms are
registered in preference order with the most preferable first.
.PP
\&\s-1RFC 8879\s0 defines zlib, brotli and zstd compression algorithms corresponding to
the following compression algorithm:
.IP "TLSEXT_cert_compression_zlib" 4
.IX Item "TLSEXT_cert_compression_zlib"
\&\s-1ZLIB\s0 compression algorithm, as defined in \s-1RFC1950.\s0
.IP "TLSEXT_cert_compression_brotli" 4
.IX Item "TLSEXT_cert_compression_brotli"
Brotli compression algorithm, as defined in \s-1RFC7932.\s0
.IP "TLSEXT_cert_compression_zstd" 4
.IX Item "TLSEXT_cert_compression_zstd"
Zstandard compression algorithm, as defined in \s-1RFC8478.\s0
.PP
The algorithm id, 1\-255 should be allocated under \*(L"\s-1IETF\s0 Review\*(R", under
\&\*(L"Specification Required\*(R" policy for values 256\-16383, 16384\-65535 can be used
for user-defined compression algorithms or others.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_get_cert_compression_compress_id()\fR returns the identifier of compression
algorithm which has been used.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_get_cert_compression_decompress_id()\fR returns the identifier of
decompression algorithm which has been used.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
\&\fBSSL_add_cert_compression_alg()\fR and \fBSSL_CTX_add_cert_compression_alg()\fR return
1 on success or 0 on error.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_get_cert_compression_compress_id()\fR return the used identifier of
compression algorithm, if no compression algorithm is used, 0 is
returned.
.PP
\&\fBSSL_get_cert_compression_decompress_id()\fR return the used identifier of
decompression algorithm, if no decompression algorithm is used, 0 is
returned.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBssl\fR\|(7)
